  MEDIUM

SearchKeys:
  rust
  embedded
  kernel
  no-std
  bare metal
  firmware

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: ADOPTED

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/languages/rust/L5-embedded-kernel.md

Evidence:
  - Embedded Rust Book
  - Rust for Embedded
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [R1] Use `#![no_std]` for embedded targets.
  [R2] Use `embedded-hal` traits for hardware abstraction.
  [R3] Use `heapless` for no-std data structures.
  [R4] Minimize dynamic allocation.
  [R5] Use `volatile` for memory-mapped registers.
  [R6] Document all `unsafe` blocks.
  [R7] Use `#[inline(always)]` sparingly.
  [R8] Test on real hardware, not just QEMU.

Pros:
  - Memory safety in low-level code
  - No segfaults
  - Modern tooling

Cons:
  - Limited ecosystem
  - steep learning curve
  - Hardware-specific code

Alternatives:
  - C (traditional)
  - C++ (RAII)
  - Zig (simpler)

State: +

